WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.632
Tom manages a research lab, and the science is the easy part.

2
00:00:05.682 --> 00:00:13.315
Tuesday morning, a technician stops him by the window: her mother is in and out of the hospital,

3
00:00:13.365 --> 00:00:20.759
she might need time, she is not sure yet, and she did not want him to think she was slacking.

4
00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:25.801
Here is job two, take care of your people, in one conversation.

5
00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:34.284
Listen and help: Tom listens, moves the two deadlines she has this week, and does not ask for a diagnosis.

6
00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:43.088
Then he routes it: one message to the leave office that afternoon, so the options are ready if she needs them.

7
00:00:43.138 --> 00:00:50.851
That is the line every manager learns: you adjust the load, the leave office decides eligibility,

8
00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:55.814
the same day. The rest of job two is smaller and just as real.

9
00:00:55.864 --> 00:01:03.817
Grow them: Tom lets the postdoc lead at the microscope and asks a question instead of answering one.

10
00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:11.820
Thank them: at the lab meeting, one technician, by name, for the specific thing she did on Thursday.

11
00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.462
Great job everyone thanks nobody.

12
00:01:14.512 --> 00:01:21.985
Trust them: he hands over the bench setup, the decision and not just the task, and steps back.

13
00:01:22.035 --> 00:01:26.547
A week later the technician is back, greeted at the door.

14
00:01:26.597 --> 00:01:31.989
People stay, and do their best work, for a manager who notices them.

15
00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:36.071
This week: thank one person for one specific thing.

